The validation APK installed successfully and retained the all-files app-op. Its
nativeLibraryDir artifact is executable and reports FFmpeg 8.1.2. The preceding
integration APK (SHA-256 a42912c3bbab61e5d7a9061bafacdf617e4be4975c9781f606b729ae238829e9)
cold-launched in 621 ms without an AndroidRuntime exception. Its main screen
reported ffmpeg-8.1.2_arm64-v8a (built-in), loaded the packaged sample metadata,
displayed the AI entry, and selected the H.264 MediaCodec hardware preset.

The installed nativeLibraryDir executable was then run under the debug package
UID with run-as. One-second 640x360/30 H.264 and HEVC clips were encoded with
explicit c2.qti.avc.encoder and c2.qti.hevc.encoder component locks. Hardware
decode selected c2.qti.avc.decoder and c2.qti.hevc.decoder; both runs decoded
30/30 frames with zero decode errors and exit status 0. Temporary private test
outputs were removed after verification.

After the Basic command builder was changed from -hwaccel auto to explicit
-hwaccel mediacodec for MediaCodec encoder presets, its equivalent final argv
was run under the same application UID. FFmpeg selected h264_mediacodec and
c2.qti.avc.decoder, then encoded HEVC with c2.qti.hevc.encoder. The 12-frame
hardware-decode-to-hardware-encode run completed with exit status 0.

