This b06219d3... artifact predates compiler path sanitization. The final
checked-in native artifact is rebuilt from the same pinned FFmpeg commit and
the same three patch contents with compiler prefix maps; codec behavior and
the functional source inputs are unchanged.

$ ANDROID_SERIAL=<device-serial> ./native/ffmpeg/test-mediacodec-encoder-matrix.sh

H.264 and HEVC each passed synchronous and asynchronous NDK encoding for
yuv420p 640x360, nv12 640x360, and yuv420p 638x358. Every case locked the
matching c2.qti hardware encoder, selected the c2.qti hardware decoder, and
decoded 30/30 frames. Raw H.264 also completed with 30/30 frames.

The MediaCodec surface chain decoded H.264 with c2.qti.avc.decoder, encoded
HEVC with c2.qti.hevc.encoder, and verified the HEVC output through
c2.qti.hevc.decoder. Both ndk_async=0 and ndk_async=1 completed with 30/30
frames. Encoder input-buffer validation checks passed throughout the matrix.
Exit status: 0

The smoke inventory for this SoC exposes c2.qti.avc.encoder/decoder and
c2.qti.hevc.encoder/decoder as hardware components. AV1 encode selects the
Android reference c2.android.av1.encoder software component; AV1 decode
selects the c2.qti.av1.decoder hardware component.
